<p>Sedation dentistry — sometimes called <strong>"sleep dentistry"</strong> — uses medication to keep you calm and comfortable during treatment. Depending on the option, you'll feel anywhere from mildly relaxed to deeply at ease, so a visit you've been dreading becomes something you can get through with no stress.</p>

<h2>Our sedation options</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Nitrous oxide ("laughing gas").</strong> Inhaled, mild, takes effect within minutes and wears off in minutes. You can drive yourself home.</li>
  <li><strong>Oral conscious sedation.</strong> A prescription pill taken before your appointment. You'll feel deeply relaxed and a little drowsy. Needs a ride home.</li>
  <li><strong>IV sedation.</strong> Medication delivered through an IV by a trained provider. Deeper relaxation, typically used for longer or more complex visits like full-arch implant surgery. Needs a ride home.</li>
</ul>

<h2>When sedation makes sense</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Significant dental anxiety or a difficult dental history</li>
  <li>Long appointments combining several procedures</li>
  <li>Full-arch implant cases (<a href="/services/all-on-4/">All-on-4 / All-on-X</a>)</li>
  <li>Complex extractions or grafting</li>
  <li>A strong gag reflex</li>
</ul>

<h2>Safety</h2>
<p>Every sedation patient is monitored throughout the visit. We review your medical history, current medications, and any concerns before we begin. If sedation isn't appropriate for you medically, we'll tell you and suggest alternatives.</p>

<h2>What to expect on the day</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Before:</strong> follow the eating and medication instructions we give you, wear comfortable clothing, and bring your driver if you're having oral or IV sedation.</li>
  <li><strong>During:</strong> we check your vital signs throughout, and Dr. Phillips explains each step if you want to know what's happening.</li>
  <li><strong>After:</strong> you rest in the office until you're steady, then go home with your driver. Plan to take it easy for the rest of the day.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Sedation for implants, extractions and full-arch treatment</h2>
<p>Many of our larger treatments are done with sedation. Every <a href="/services/dentures/">full-mouth denture and implant package</a> we offer includes IV sedation, along with all extractions. Sedation is also common for <a href="/services/wisdom-teeth-removal/">wisdom teeth removal</a>, <a href="/services/tooth-extractions/">surgical extractions</a> and <a href="/services/all-on-4/">All-on-4</a> surgery, where it lets us complete more in one visit.</p>

<h2>Talk to us about dental anxiety</h2>
<p>You don't have to explain or apologize for being nervous. Tell us what's been hard for you in the past, whether it's needles, sounds, gagging or a bad experience, and we'll plan around it. Sometimes a slower pace, more breaks and a clear explanation help as much as medication.</p>

